      },
      "text": "The printing press was not a single invention — it was a system of five interlocking innovations that together created a manufacturing process for text. Gutenberg did not invent moveable type; he invented the first production-quality, economically viable system for mass-producing accurate type at the speed required to make printing commercially feasible."
